uests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Criterion 5 must define the key-count target against the set of tests that ACTUALLY RAN under the pinned default selection (accounting for importorskip/deselected/xfail nodes), not raw collected node count, and name the environment (installed extras) the capture is taken in.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5: '.test_durations is committed for the default selection with a key count equal to the collected node count'","tests/unit shows many pytest.importorskip('pydantic_ai'), importorskip('fastapi'), importorskip('httpx') gates — these COLLECT but SKIP, producing no duration key when the dep is absent","pytest-split records durations per executed call phase, not per collected node"],"finding":"Criterion 5 requires .test_durations to be committed 'with a key count equal to the collected node count', but pytest-split's .test_durations only records a duration key for tests that actually EXECUTED. The suite is dense with pytest.importorskip-gated and extra-gated tests (pydantic_ai, fastapi, httpx) that SKIP under the lean default selection, so collected-count and recorded-key-count diverge by the number of skipped/deselected/xfail nodes. The equality invariant is therefore either unachievable or silently depends on which optional deps are installed in the capture environment.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c46ce00bad354b3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, criterion 5 (durations story / S5)","norm_id":"ne6f2c00f8774cee2","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Capture environment lacks the [ui]/pydantic_ai extras: dozens of nodes collect but skip, key count < collected count, AC5 fails","AC5's equality check becomes a flaky function of the capture host's installed extras"],"severity":null,"sugge