g `.test_durations` in docs/local-dev-env.md. It does not state that the new TID251/TID253 contract is documented, nor that docs/AGENTS.md references to the deleted scan modules / retired parity test / relocated scripts are swept so no stale reference survives.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f48560297decc9bd2","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, criteria 4 and 5; Context final paragraph","norm_id":"n926086e86e5759e4","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A developer hits a new TID251/TID253 ruff failure and finds no documented rationale for the import ban","A doc or AGENTS.md still points to a deleted scan module or the retired test_ci_workflow_parity.py after the epic lands"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Criterion 4 must distinguish the STATIC AST scan (replaced by TID251) from the dynamic subprocess collection test(s) in test_tests_import_convention.py, and state that trapped behaviour tests (e.g. test_audit_page_modules_collect_under_bare_pytest) are MOVED/kept, not deleted with the scan.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC4: 'the two AST scans they replace are deleted'","test_tests_import_convention.py:82 test_audit_page_modules_collect_under_bare_pytest runs `console_script ... --collect-only` in a subprocess with PYTHONPATH stripped — a dynamic reproduction TID251 cannot express","The epic's stated philosophy elsewhere is to RECOVER trapped behaviour tests, not delete them (criterion 1: '39 moved')"],"finding":"Criterion 4 says 'the two AST scans they replace are deleted', but test_tests_import_convention.py (the TID251 scan) also contains a dynamic behaviour test — test_audit_page_modules_collect_under_bare_pytest — that subprocess-runs the bare `pytest --collect-only` console script to prove bug a371's collection failure cannot regress. ruff's flake8-tidy-imports (TID251) is a purely static lint and cannot reproduce that runtime collection check, so deleting the whole module loses a genuine regression anchor the rest of this epic is explicitly designed to preserve (S1 moves trapped behaviour tests rather than deleting them).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8c17a3e03bc7bc04","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, criterion 4 (ruff story / S4)","norm_id":"n6da61f339259405a","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["S4 deletes test_tests_import_convention.py wholesale and the bug-a371 bare-pytest collection regression is no longer guarded by any test"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC4 to 'the two STATIC AST scans are deleted and any trapped behaviour test (bare-pytest collection reproduction for bug a371) is moved to a surviving module', mirroring the S1 move-not-delete rule.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context"